course: dictionary
lesson: 1494
title: Cavern: a large, hollow space
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: In the snowy wood there were «snow-castles and snow-caverns». Snow-castles are castles made of snow, so snow-caverns must be hollow spaces made of snow, like little caves.
explain: A cavern is a large cave, often deep under the ground. The word can also mean any large, dark, empty space that feels like a cave. The adjective cavernous describes something huge and hollow, like a cavern.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "cave" in place of "cavern" in a sentence. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A cavern is a large cave, often deep under the ground.
fact: A cavern can also be any large, dark, empty space that feels like a cave.
fact: In science, caverns form when water slowly dissolves limestone over thousands of years.
fact: In stories, caverns are often full of dragons, treasure and danger.
fact: Cavernous is the adjective: a cavernous space is huge and hollow.
exercise: «There were snow-castles and snow-caverns in the snowy wood.» What does cavern mean? | A bright, sunny meadow | A small tent for camping | *A large cave, often deep under the ground | A tall tower built of stone
exercise: In geography, how do caverns form? | *Water slowly dissolves limestone over thousands of years | Strong winds blow the rock away in one day | Volcanoes melt the stone into a hole | Children dig them with spades in the sand
exercise: Which word is the adjective form of cavern? | *cavernous | caveman | cavity | cavern-like
test: Hikers lit torches to explore the vast cavern. What does vast mean here? | *Very large | Very cold | Very small | Very wet
test: Ellie says a cavern is just a cupboard. Which meaning is right? | A wooden stick for walking | *A huge hollow space that feels like a cave | A small cupboard for toys | A kind of bird that lives in trees
exam: Which word means a large, dark, empty space that feels like a cave? | Carpet | Candle | *Cavern | Cupboard
